
assignment: make a structural time series model and predict primary production based on the model

input: 
- pp_wide.csv (primary production parameters and environments; example file)
- knmi_daily.csv (with daily irradiance)
- pp_validation (depth integrated pp observations) (not independent, for they are calcualated using the same EP model, but with measured parameters)

Parameters have the following units
   parameter           unit                                       
 1 chlfa               ug/l                                       
 2 turbidity           NTU                                        
 3 O2                  mg/l                                       
 4 perc_O2             %                                          
 5 salinity            PSU                                        
 6 PP_depth_integrated mg C/m2/d                                  
 7 PBmax_EP            mgC (mg chla)-1 h-1                        
 8 alfaB_EP            mgC (mg chla)-1 h-1)/(µmol fotonen m-2 s-1)
 9 Eopt_EP             µmol fotonen m-2 s-1                       
10 pH                  pH_units                                   
11 irradiance_J_cm2    J/cm2              
12 bottomdepth         m                                          
13 Kd                  /m                                         
14 conversionEtoC      molC/(mol fotons)       

do
- calculate incident PAR from irradiance

make functions 
- "fit_model"
- "make_predictions"

use R tidyverse and tidymodel workflows

fit parameters:
- PBmax
- alpha
- Eopt
- Kd
- Chl_surface (chlorophyll a in ug/l)

include:
- seasonal spline
- long term spline
- method to include the spring bloom dynamics (depending on compartment, usually a short burst of chlfa around March each year)

Make model per compartment

use fitted parameters to calculate daily primary production using an Eilers Peters model with photoinhibition using
- fitparameters
- irradiance (for each day)

Add Shapley decomposition in three components 
- long term 
- seasonal
- spring bloom


make plots of:
- time series depth integrated daily modelled pp and daily observed pp
- diagnostics
- observed vs predicted and residuals plot for all parameters






Then: include also alternative measurments for chlfa and Kd (from MWTL)


